Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:45:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] module: accept modversion CRCs from the ROM vendor modules

The RisingOS OTA modules carry CRCs generated from a kernel tree with
KSU/SUSFS headers. They share our vermagic but disagree on many symbol
CRCs, so the stock loader rejects them. For the compatibility profile,
accept those CRCs instead of replacing the ROM modules.
---
--- a/kernel/module/version.c
+++ b/kernel/module/version.c
@@ -19,6 +19,10 @@
 	unsigned int versindex = info->index.vers;
 	unsigned int i, num_versions;
 	struct modversion_info *versions;
+	/* RisingOS drop-in: vendor modules were built against the ROM kernel
+	 * tree with KSU/SUSFS headers. Keep vermagic identical, but accept
+	 * their modversion CRCs so those modules can still be loaded. */
+	return 1;
 
 	/* Exporting module didn't supply crcs?  OK, we're already tainted. */
 	if (!crc)
